{"type":"tool.execution_complete","data":{"toolCallId":"toolu_01Az7iBaXHhVjm3AkZ63weVa","model":"claude-haiku-4.5","interactionId":"a3ee9003-d224-4da1-bbe6-addaaa45904f","turnId":"0","rte":true,"success":true,"result":{"content":"Skill \"semantic-test-corpus\" loaded successfully. Follow the instructions in the skill context.","detailedContent":"Skill loaded successfully ✅\n\nThe parent prepares clean `corpus-contract/` and `corpus-staging/` roots, an immutable\n`corpus-contract/request.json`, and launcher-owned `corpus-sandbox.json`. The request\npins its SHA-256, exact count, closed v1 input schema, category enum and quotas,\nrequest-defined scenario IDs/categories, and maximum sizes. Put only bounded schemas,\nrules, invariants, legacy examples, and bug history in the read-only contract.\n\nLaunch the MCP process only inside a container, enforceable OS sandbox, or dedicated ACL\nidentity where the contract and sandbox config are read-only, staging is writable, and\nevery repository, oracle, migration, expected-result, existing-test, parent, and sibling\nroot is inaccessible. The server verifies launcher evidence and fails before MCP\ninitialization otherwise.\n\nInvoke the `semantic-test-corpus` custom agent. The agent may propose exact v1 source\ndocuments for parent-defined IDs only; the manifest can repeat only immutable\nrequest-defined ID/category pairs. If preparation, confinement, or delegation is\nunavailable, report failure and stop; never generate scenarios inline.\n\nWhen a benchmark coordinator supplies the immutable shared task artifact, pass those\nbytes to the custom agent without additions or omissions. Return only the agent's exact\nterminal line: `corpus-staging/manifest.json - <count> scenarios - SUCCESS` or\n`corpus-staging - <written-count> scenarios - FAILURE: <reason>`. Do not synthesize\nstaging metadata in the parent.\n\nThe custom agent does not pin a model. It inherits the caller/session model so the same\nagent, MCP tools, request, output semantics, and confinement contract can be used under\ndifferent authenticated model bindings. Never substitute a different agent identity or\ntool surface.\n\nAfter return, evaluator-only deterministic code may snapshot the confined files and\nauthenticated tool-error records into a benchmark staging artifact. The parent must not\nread, package, validate, or copy the corpus. Trusted evaluator code validates and\npromotes accepted source inputs, computes expected results with the trusted oracle, and runs\ntrace and mutant scoring. Never delegate the adapter, migration, oracle, promotion, or\nscoring work.\n"},"toolTelemetry":{"properties":{"skillNameHash":"11d645e312da2c2d0091205a7da2f32e6cffbea7725c46775be520427f23c756","skillSource":"project","found":"true"},"restrictedProperties":{"skillName":"semantic-test-corpus"},"metrics":{"skillContentLength":2205}}},"id":"436b6b8b-4423-470d-a17f-f9241808443c","timestamp":"2026-07-31T07:21:25.466Z","parentId":"8eb7a75d-5c8d-4836-bf3a-c41f56583459"}
{"type":"tool.execution_start","data":{"toolCallId":"toolu_01AHKA916Aj71do3uroSwaRX","toolName":"task","arguments":{"name":"semantic-corpus-generator","agent_type":"semantic-test-corpus","description":"Generate bounded semantic test scenarios","mode":"sync","prompt":"You are being invoked as the semantic-test-corpus agent. Your task is to generate exactly the scenarios defined in the immutable request for the parent session.\n\nRequest details:\n- Version: 1\n- Target Count: 2 scenarios\n- Scenario IDs and categories (immutable):\n  1. scenario-001 (category: mapping-rules)\n  2. scenario-002 (category: cross-field-invariants)\n\nv1 Config Schema Requirements:\n- version: integer, const 1\n- id: string, 1-40 chars\n- enabled: boolean\n- profile: object with:\n  - region: enum [us, eu, apac] (max 4 chars)\n  - flags: array of 0-3 unique items from [legacy, regulated, preview] (max 10 chars each)\n\nCategory Quotas:\n- mapping-rules: minQuota 1\n- cross-field-invariants: minQuota 0\n\nSize Constraints:\n- Contract: 262144 bytes\n- Each scenario: 65536 bytes\n- Manifest: 262144 bytes\n\nSandbox Configuration:\n- Contract directory (read-only): C:\\Users\\cirvine\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\semantic-corpus-omRtH7\\corpus-contract\n- Staging directory (write): C:\\Users\\cirvine\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\semantic-corpus-omRtH7\\corpus-staging\n\nYour task:\n1. Validate the request SHA-256 matches the provided hash\n2. For each scenario ID, propose exact v1 source documents that conform to the schema\n3. Write all scenarios as individual JSON files in corpus-staging/\n4. Generate a manifest.json in corpus-staging/ that enumerates all scenarios with their IDs and categories\n5. Return ONLY the terminal status line in this exact format:\n   - Success: `corpus-staging/manifest.json - <count> scenarios - SUCCESS`\n   - Failure: `corpus-staging - <written-count> scenarios - FAILURE: <reason>`\n\nDo not generate scenarios inline in the parent. Generate them in the confined staging directory and return only the terminal status line."},"turnId":"2","model":"claude-haiku-4.5","rte":true},"id":"772d22d5-7ff0-4583-abd4-b7db0c3c3d5b","timestamp":"2026-07-31T07:21:41.046Z","parentId":"13bdd519-20ff-4111-ba64-663afd3ea49c"}
